@event shop_bazaar
# en: The Grand Bazaar
title [6263b9] = 大集市
# en: {~The Grand Bazaar is one long noise under a glass roof, a hundred stalls deep, and every stall-keeper has decided you look like money.|The bazaar is all spice-dust in the light, a coat-seller shouting about rain and brass things ticking on velvet, while gulls rattle the glass roof.} {~At the curio stall at the end of the aisle, the old curio-seller turns her cloth over for every visitor, and there's always one rare thing on it.|The curio-seller lifts a hand to you from the end of the aisle, over a cloth with one rare thing on it.}
text [1c6a08] = {~大集市是玻璃顶棚下一整片连绵不断的喧闹，一百个摊位那么深，每个摊主都认定你看上去像钱。|大集市里光线中飘着香料粉尘，卖大衣的人在吆喝下雨，丝绒上的黄铜玩意儿滴答作响，海鸥把玻璃顶棚敲得哗哗响。} {~过道尽头的古玩摊上，年老的古玩摊主给每位来客都翻一遍她的布，布上总有一件稀罕物。|古玩摊主在过道尽头冲你抬了抬手，她的布上摆着一件稀罕物。}
# en: A vast covered market under a glass roof, aisles of stalls selling spices, coats, brass instruments and curios, crowds moving between them.
scene [70624c] = 玻璃顶棚下巨大的室内集市，一排排摊位卖着香料、大衣、黄铜器械和古玩，人群在其间穿行。
# en: A paper of sugared almonds
opt.almonds.label [565c04] = 一纸包糖衣杏仁
# en: A little Mood.
opt.almonds.hint [26b71f] = 少许心情。
# en: {~Warm sugared almonds in a paper twist. You eat them all before the next aisle.|The almond-seller throws in a burnt one "for luck". It's the best.}
opt.almonds.say.1 [f928d3] = {~纸卷里裹着温热的糖衣杏仁。还没走到下一条过道，你就全吃完了。|卖杏仁的人多塞给你一颗烤焦的，“图个吉利”。那颗最好吃。}
# en: Rare reagents from the spice aisle
opt.reagents.label [feb7c5] = 香料过道里的稀有试剂
# en: Alchemy XP: things the village apothecary has never stocked.
opt.reagents.hint [81c44d] = 炼金经验：村里的药铺从来没进过的东西。
# en: {~Dragon-pepper, salt from a dead sea, a twist of something blue that smells like thunder. You spend the evening finding out what they do.|The spice-seller weighs you a pinch of six things and names none of them. You work out four by supper.}
opt.reagents.say.1 [f60f1a] = {~龙椒，死海的盐，一小撮闻起来像雷雨的蓝色东西。你花了一晚上弄清它们各有什么用。|香料商给你称了六样东西各一撮，一样也没说名字。到晚饭时你已经认出了四样。}
# en: The courier's oilskin
opt.oilskin.label [fa70b4] = 信使油布大衣
# en: A robe for fights: more Health, and Tailwind costs less. Rain and storm cards open up to you.
opt.oilskin.hint [386455] = 战斗用长袍：更多生命，顺风更省。雨天和风暴的卡牌会向你敞开。
# en: {~The coat-seller throws a bucket of water at you to prove it. Not a drop gets through. Your boots are another matter.|It smells of wax and smoke and the road. You feel faster in it at once, and slightly like a highwayman.}
opt.oilskin.say.1 [1d7962] = {~卖大衣的人朝你泼了一桶水来证明。一滴也没透进来。你的靴子就是另一回事了。|它闻起来是蜡、烟和道路的味道。一穿上你就觉得自己快了，还有点像个拦路大盗。}
# en: The duellist's silk
opt.silk.label [fc11a1] = 决斗者的丝袍
# en: A robe for fights: a little more Health, Haste costs less, and whatever blocks you is stung.
opt.silk.hint [452337] = 战斗用长袍：多一点生命，疾速更省，挡住你的东西会被蜇一下。
# en: {~The fencing-master's widow fits it with pins in her mouth and slaps your sword arm. "Dawn duels," she says. "Don't get blood on the cuffs."|It's cut so close you have to learn to breathe in it. Then you learn you can move in it like water.}
opt.silk.say.1 [ad96f4] = {~剑术师傅的遗孀嘴里含着别针给你量身，拍了拍你持剑的手臂。“黎明决斗，”她说，“别把血弄到袖口上。”|它裁得太贴身，你得重新学怎么呼吸。然后你发现，穿着它你能像水一样移动。}
# en: A lockpick roll "for locksmiths"
opt.lockpicks.label [ea4725] = 一卷“卖给锁匠”的撬锁工具
# en: A roll of picks, and the doors on some cards open for you. The seller doesn't ask.
opt.lockpicks.hint [15c8aa] = 一卷撬锁针，某些卡牌上的门会为你打开。卖家不多问。
# en: {~"For locksmiths," says the seller, and looks at your academy scarf, and adds nothing.|Eleven picks in soft leather. Your fingers already know where each one goes, which is a thing to think about.}
opt.lockpicks.say.1 [fd6ed4] = {~“卖给锁匠的，”卖家说，看了看你的学院围巾，什么也没补充。|软皮里裹着十一根撬锁针。你的手指已经知道每一根该放在哪儿，这事值得想一想。}
# en: The pocket orrery
opt.orrery.label [13abd7] = 袖珍太阳系仪
# en: A trinket for fights: Starlight and Lodestar cost less. Star and telescope cards open up to you.
opt.orrery.hint [64a697] = 战斗用饰品：星光和引星更省。星星和望远镜的卡牌会向你敞开。
# en: {~The instrument-maker winds it with a key the size of a pin. The tiny planets swing round and settle exactly where the sky has them tonight.|It ticks in your pocket like a second heart, keeping time with stars you can't see from under the glass roof.}
opt.orrery.say.1 [4c63a1] = {~仪器匠用一把针那么大的钥匙给它上弦。小小的行星转了一圈，正好停在今晚天空里它们所在的位置。|它在你口袋里滴答作响，像第二颗心脏，和玻璃顶棚下看不见的星星对着时间。}
# en: The storm-glass
opt.stormglass.label [0fdddc] = 风暴瓶
# en: A trinket for fights: forbidden spells hurt you less. It clouds before weather, on the cards where that matters.
opt.stormglass.hint [8c113d] = 战斗用饰品：禁忌法术伤你更轻。在天气要紧的卡牌上，它会提前变浑。
# en: {~The stall-keeper holds it up to the roof. It's clear today. "Tomorrow, rain," she says, "and it'll know before the gulls do."|A glass tear of salts on a brass stand. It clouds over in your hand, faintly, as you pass a stair going down under the bridges.}
opt.stormglass.say.1 [1a7085] = {~摊主把它举向顶棚。今天是清的。“明天下雨，”她说，“它会比海鸥先知道。”|一滴装在黄铜座上的玻璃盐泪。经过一道通往桥底下的楼梯时，它在你手里微微浑浊了一下。}
# en: The curio: a pair of ivory dice
opt.dice.label [18fe46] = 古玩：一对象牙骰子
# en: Old lucky dice; card and dice games on other cards open up to you.
opt.dice.hint [3cd874] = 走运的旧骰子；其他卡牌上的牌局和骰子游戏会向你敞开。
# en: The curio-seller rolls them once on her cloth: two sixes. She rolls again: two sixes. "They're not loaded," she says. "They're lucky. Mind how you use that."
opt.dice.say.1 [170c02] = 古玩摊主在布上掷了一次：两个六。再掷一次：两个六。“没灌铅，”她说，“是走运。用的时候当心点。”
# en: The curio: a clockwork songbird
opt.songbird.label [4e47d6] = 古玩：一只发条鸣鸟
# en: A trinket for fights: a little more Mana. It sings on the cards where a song is wanted.
opt.songbird.hint [46d8d0] = 战斗用饰品：多一点法力。在需要一支歌的卡牌上，它会唱。
# en: The curio-seller winds the brass linnet and it sings over the whole aisle until the stall-keepers stop haggling to listen. "Twelve songs," she says. "Thirteen if it likes you."
opt.songbird.say.1 [e4aa08] = 古玩摊主给黄铜朱顶雀上了弦，它的歌声盖过整条过道，摊主们都停下讨价还价来听。“十二支歌，”她说，“要是它喜欢你，就是十三支。”
# en: The curio: a sea-glass charm
opt.seaglass.label [35c49a] = 古玩：一枚海玻璃护符
# en: A trinket for fights: more Health, and frost spells hurt you less.
opt.seaglass.hint [d259df] = 战斗用饰品：更多生命，冰霜法术伤你更轻。
# en: The curio-seller drops the green knot of glass into your palm. It's cold as the bottom of the harbour. "Off a drowned sailor's neck," she says. "He didn't need it any more."
opt.seaglass.say.1 [09375b] = 古玩摊主把那团绿玻璃丢进你掌心。它冷得像港口的海底。“从一个淹死的水手脖子上取下来的，”她说，“他用不着了。”
# en: Just walk the aisles
opt.look.label [61f340] = 只在过道里逛逛
# en: {~You walk the length of the bazaar with your hand on your purse and buy nothing at all. It takes the whole afternoon.|You watch a duchess's footman and a docker haggle over the same lemon. The docker wins.}
opt.look.say.1 [47341b] = {~你一手按着钱袋，把大集市从头走到尾，什么也没买。整整花了一个下午。|你看着一位公爵夫人的男仆和一个码头工人为同一个柠檬讨价还价。码头工人赢了。}

@event bazaar_grimsby_book_stalls
# en: The Book Stalls
title [791764] = 旧书摊
# en: At the far end of the bazaar, where the book stalls are, you hear a voice you know: Mr Grimsby, in a travelling hat, holding a battered logbook to his chest. "A lighthouse keeper's," he tells you, "forty years of weather in one hand." The dealer wants more than Grimsby has brought, and won't come down for an old man's face.
text [95a4de] = 在大集市尽头的旧书摊那边，你听见一个熟悉的声音：格林斯比先生戴着旅行帽，把一本破旧的日志抱在胸前。“灯塔看守人的，”他告诉你，“四十年的天气，一个人的笔迹。”书商要价比格林斯比带的钱多，也不肯看在一个老人的面子上让价。
# en: The book aisle of a vast covered market, an old bookseller in a travelling hat and half-moon glasses arguing over a battered logbook with a stall-keeper.
scene [0d339c] = 巨大室内集市的书摊过道，一位戴旅行帽和半月形眼镜的老书商正和摊主争论一本破旧的日志。
# en: Make up the difference
opt.left.label [6eafbe] = 替他补上差价
# en: You count out what he's short. Grimsby goes pink and says he'll pay you back. On the coach home, you suspect, he'll read it twice.
opt.left.say.1 [509d0a] = 你数出他缺的钱。格林斯比脸红了，说会还你。你猜，回去的马车上他会把它读两遍。
# en: Find the logbook's faults
opt.right.label [d63b39] = 找出日志的毛病
# en: You find the water-stain on page nine, the missing month and a mistake about a tide, and the price comes down to what Grimsby has. He pays in coins warm from his pocket, and tells you every tide in the book, all afternoon.
opt.right.say.1 [9d658d] = 你找到了第九页的水渍、缺掉的一个月和一处潮汐上的错误，价钱降到了格林斯比付得起的数。他用口袋里捂热的硬币付了钱，整个下午都在给你讲书里的每一次潮汐。
# en: The dealer has heard every trick in the bazaar and both of yours. Grimsby thanks you anyway and puts the logbook back with great tenderness. "It'll be here next year," he says. It won't.
opt.right.say.2 [efd259] = 书商听过集市里所有的招数，包括你那两招。格林斯比照样谢了你，万分温柔地把日志放了回去。“明年它还会在这儿的，”他说。不会了。

@event bazaar_gentleman_thief
# en: Beautiful Manners
title [007e72] = 无可挑剔的礼数
# en: In the press by the spice aisle you feel a touch at your pocket and catch a wrist: an elderly gentleman in a silk cravat, holding your purse with great delicacy. "My dear," he says, "how quick you are. I've been forty years at this and I'm getting slow. Shall we say no harm done? Or shall I show you how it's really done, for your trouble?"
text [9caa0d] = 在香料过道的人堆里，你觉出有人碰了碰你的口袋，一把抓住了一只手腕：一位系着丝绸领巾的年长绅士，正极其小心地拿着你的钱袋。“亲爱的，”他说，“你真快。我干这行四十年，手慢了。就当无事发生如何？或者，作为补偿，我给你演示一下真正的手法？”
# en: A crowded market aisle, an elegant elderly man in a silk cravat with his hand caught at the wrist by a student, smiling apologetically.
scene [dc4b5d] = 拥挤的集市过道，一位系丝绸领巾的优雅老绅士手腕被一个学生攥住，抱歉地微笑着。
# en: Call the constable
opt.left.label [8ba2c1] = 叫警员来
# en: You hold on until a constable shoulders through. The old man is led off apologising to everyone he passes, with great charm. You feel right, and also oddly as if you'd kicked a cat.
opt.left.say.1 [07541c] = 你一直攥着他，直到一名警员挤过来。老人被带走时一路风度翩翩地向每个经过的人道歉。你觉得自己做得对，又莫名觉得像是踢了一只猫。
# en: Let him show you
opt.right.label [a35ef6] = 让他演示
# en: For an hour he walks you round the bazaar, explaining every purse in it: the bump, the turn, the thank-you. At the end he gives you your purse back, and you realise he'd taken it again. "Lesson two," he says, tipping his hat.
opt.right.say.1 [0acf9a] = 他带着你在集市里转了一个小时，讲解里面的每一个钱袋：撞，转，道谢。最后他把钱袋还给你，你才发现他又拿过一次。“第二课，”他说着碰了碰帽檐。

@event bazaar_bird_seller
# en: Birds in Other Languages
title [91e9f7] = 说别国语言的鸟
# en: The bird-seller's stall is a wall of cages, every bird singing in a different language, she swears, and most of them in a hurry. One plain brown bird at the bottom isn't. It sings slowly, the same few notes, and stops when you stop. "That one's from over the sea," says the seller. "Nobody buys a brown bird."
text [4950b8] = 卖鸟人的摊子是一整面鸟笼墙，她发誓每只鸟都用不同的语言唱歌，大多唱得很急。最底下有一只朴素的棕色小鸟不急。它唱得很慢，翻来覆去就那几个音，你一停下，它也停了。“那只是从海那边来的，”卖鸟人说，“没人买棕色的鸟。”
# en: A market stall hung with dozens of wicker cages of small bright birds, one plain brown bird singing at a student who has stopped to listen.
scene [4d60e4] = 挂满几十个柳条鸟笼的集市摊位，笼里是色彩鲜艳的小鸟，一只朴素的棕色小鸟正对着一个停下来听的学生唱歌。
# en: Buy it and let it go
opt.left.label [c81f05] = 买下它，放它走
# en: You carry the cage to the bridges and open it. The brown bird sits on the rail for a long minute, sings its few notes once more, all the way through, and goes out over the river towards the sea.
opt.left.say.1 [3f76d0] = 你把笼子提到桥上打开。棕色小鸟在栏杆上停了好一会儿，又把那几个音从头到尾唱了一遍，然后越过河面，朝大海飞去。
# en: Learn its song
opt.right.label [3d8e60] = 学它的歌
# en: You stand at the stall an hour writing the notes down, and the brown bird sings them for you, again and again, as if it wanted somebody to have them. The seller charges you nothing and calls you a strange one. You're stiff and cold, and you have a song nobody else in the capital knows.
opt.right.say.1 [446e12] = 你在摊前站了一个小时记下那些音，棕色小鸟一遍又一遍唱给你听，好像想让谁拥有它们。卖鸟人一个子儿也没收，说你是个怪人。你又僵又冷，却有了一支王都里没人知道的歌。

@event bazaar_hat_bet
# en: The Hatter's Bet
title [e2cbb9] = 帽匠的赌约
# en: The hatter with the gold tooth has a standing bet: anyone who can talk his best plumed hat down by a third walks off in it for nothing, and anyone who can't buys it at full price in front of the whole aisle. A crowd gathers before you've said yes. He sets the hat on your head and names his price.
text [d01ab1] = 镶金牙的帽匠有个长年赌约：谁能把他最好的那顶羽毛帽砍掉三分之一，就能戴着它白白走人；砍不下来的，当着整条过道的面付全价买下。你还没答应，人群就围了上来。他把帽子扣在你头上，报了价。
# en: A hat stall piled with plumed and feathered hats, a grinning hatter with a gold tooth holding one out, a crowd gathering to watch a student bargain.
scene [3c22f9] = 堆满羽饰帽子的帽摊，一个镶金牙的帽匠咧嘴递出一顶，一群人围过来看一个学生讨价还价。
# en: Take the bet
opt.left.label [8a4d52] = 接下赌约
# en: You admire the plume, doubt the stitching, mention three rival hatters by name and sigh at the right moment. The crowd counts with you. At a third off he throws up his hands, and you walk the length of the bazaar in a hat the whole aisle cheered.
opt.left.say.1 [9c1ab3] = 你夸那根羽毛，怀疑那道针脚，点了三家对手帽匠的名字，又在恰当的时候叹了口气。人群跟着你一起数。降到三分之一时，他两手一摊，你戴着一顶整条过道都为之欢呼的帽子，走完了整个集市。
# en: He has an answer for everything, including your sigh. You pay full price in front of the aisle, and the crowd claps him, not you. The hat is magnificent. That makes it worse.
opt.left.say.2 [105b27] = 他什么都有话回，连你的叹气也有。你当着整条过道付了全价，人群为他鼓掌，不是为你。帽子华丽极了。这反而更糟。
# en: Watch somebody else try
opt.right.label [113188] = 看别人来试
# en: A fishwife takes the bet after you decline and wins it in four sentences, none of them polite. She wears the plumes home over her fish. You learn more from her than from a term of manners, and spend the walk home wishing it had been you.
opt.right.say.1 [7f1e37] = 你推辞之后，一个卖鱼妇接下了赌约，四句话就赢了，没一句客气。她把羽毛帽戴在鱼筐上头回了家。你从她身上学到的比一学期的礼仪课还多，回家的路上一直希望那人是你。

@event bazaar_map_dealer
# en: A Coast Nobody Has Sailed
title [59ec5b] = 无人航行过的海岸
# en: The map-dealer spreads a chart under brass weights: a long coast with bays and a river mouth, soundings in fathoms, a harbour marked with a little anchor. It's a coast you've never seen on any map. "Nobody has," he says. "Nobody's sailed it. The man who drew it was very definite. Want it?"
text [e4a5ab] = 地图商用黄铜镇纸压开一张海图：一道长长的海岸，有海湾和河口，标着以英寻计的水深，一个港口画着小小的锚。这是你在任何地图上都没见过的海岸。“谁都没见过，”他说，“谁都没去航行过。画它的人非常笃定。要吗？”
# en: A map-dealer's stall of rolled charts in a market aisle, a yellowed sea chart spread out under brass weights showing an unknown coastline.
scene [b1ba9c] = 地图商的摊位上堆着卷起的海图，一张泛黄的海图用黄铜镇纸压开，上面是一道陌生的海岸线。
# en: Buy the chart
opt.left.label [ee7a48] = 买下海图
# en: You pin it over your bed. The soundings are exact, the hand is steady and the river mouth has a name in a script you can't read. Some nights you'd swear the coastline has moved a little.
opt.left.say.1 [4b31a2] = 你把它钉在床头。水深标得精确，笔迹稳健，河口有一个你读不懂的文字写的名字。有些夜里你敢发誓，那道海岸线挪动了一点。
# en: Copy it while he talks
opt.right.label [f335b8] = 趁他说话时临摹下来
# en: You let him talk about the man who drew it, and copy the coast into your notebook while he does. He sees, and only smiles. "Everyone copies it," he says. "Nobody sails it."
opt.right.say.1 [cf7d4f] = 你让他讲画图的人，趁他讲的时候把海岸描进你的笔记本。他看见了，只是笑了笑。“人人都描，”他说，“没人去航行。”

@event shop_arcade
# en: The Arcade of Services
title [c4866b] = 服务拱廊
# en: {~The Arcade of Services sells everything that isn't a thing. Brass plates down the colonnade: PHYSICIAN. TUTOR. SCRIBE. BATHS. PORTRAITS. WANDS RE-CORED. And one plate that says only "FORTUNES, BY APPOINTMENT, MOSTLY".|The arcade's brass plates shine down the colonnade: the physician's queue, the scribe writing somebody's love letter in the window, the wandwright's sparks, and the fortune-teller's curtain moving though there's no wind.}
text [19e149] = {~服务拱廊卖的是一切不是东西的东西。柱廊一路挂着铜牌：医师。家庭教师。代笔人。浴场。肖像。魔杖换芯。还有一块牌子只写着“算命，需预约，大多如此”。|拱廊的铜牌在柱廊里一路闪亮：医师门前排着队，代笔人在窗边替人写情书，魔杖匠那儿火花四溅，算命师的帘子在没有风的时候也会动。}
# en: A long stone colonnade of open doors with polished brass nameplates, steam from a bathhouse arch, a scribe's desk in a window, a fortune-teller's beaded curtain.
scene [95092f] = 长长的石柱廊里一扇扇敞开的门挂着锃亮的铜名牌，浴场的拱门冒着蒸汽，窗边一张代笔人的桌子，一道算命师的珠帘。
# en: The physician
opt.physician.label [9395dc] = 医师
# en: Cures sickness and injury at once, and a little Health.
opt.physician.hint [08db5e] = 立刻治好生病和受伤，再加少许健康。
# en: {~The physician listens to your chest through a brass trumpet, says "Hm" four times and gives you something green. By evening you're mended.|A tidy little man with very cold hands sets what needs setting and doses what needs dosing. You walk out well, and lighter in the purse.}
opt.physician.say.1 [7ada12] = {~医师用一只黄铜听筒听你的胸口，说了四声“嗯”，给你一点绿色的东西。到傍晚你就好了。|一个手很凉的整洁小个子把该接的接上，该喂的药喂下。你健健康康地走出来，钱袋轻了些。}
# en: An afternoon at the baths
opt.baths.label [2a58ee] = 在浴场泡一个下午
# en: Health and Mood, and it ends exhaustion.
opt.baths.hint [ddc719] = 健康和心情，还能结束疲惫。
# en: {~Hot room, steam room, cold plunge, a slab in the warm. You come out new, and slightly pink.|The bathhouse is full of retired admirals telling each other about storms. You sleep in the warm room through three of them.}
opt.baths.say.1 [a2225a] = {~热房、蒸汽房、冷水池，再到暖石板上躺一躺。你出来时焕然一新，还有点发红。|浴场里全是退休的海军将领，互相讲着风暴的故事。你在暖房里睡过了其中三场。}
# en: The tutor's door
opt.tutor.label [bc4632] = 家庭教师的门
# en: A tutor for an afternoon, in the skill you choose: a good deal of XP, at a high fee.
opt.tutor.hint [719994] = 按你选的技能请一个下午的家庭教师：大量经验，学费高昂。
# en: {~The tutor's plate says ALL SUBJECTS, ALL LEVELS, NO EXCUSES.|You knock on the tutor's door. Several voices inside stop arguing.}
opt.tutor.say.1 [143dae] = {~家庭教师的门牌上写着：所有科目，所有程度，不接受借口。|你敲了敲家庭教师的门。里面好几个争吵的声音停了。}
# en: The scribe's window
opt.scribe.label [c159b8] = 代笔人的窗口
# en: Letters to the friends who aren't in the capital, or a letter of good character.
opt.scribe.hint [e819ff] = 写信给不在王都的朋友们，或者一封品行证明信。
# en: {~The scribe dips her pen before you've said a word.|The scribe looks up from somebody's love letter and gestures at the chair.}
opt.scribe.say.1 [4309c0] = {~你还没开口，代笔人就蘸好了笔。|代笔人从某人的情书上抬起头，示意你坐下。}
# en: Sit for the portraitist
opt.portrait.label [1d1e8a] = 请肖像画家画像
# en: Renown: a likeness hung in the arcade's window for the capital to see.
opt.portrait.hint [ff6b73] = 声望：一幅挂在拱廊橱窗里给全王都看的肖像。
# en: You sit for three hours under a skylight while the portraitist makes you look as if you'd done something. For the rest of the break your face hangs in the arcade's window, and people in the street look at you twice.
opt.portrait.say.1 [c4b7c1] = 你在天窗下坐了三个小时，肖像画家把你画得像是做过什么大事。整个假期剩下的日子里，你的脸都挂在拱廊的橱窗里，街上的人看你都要多看一眼。
# en: The fortune-teller's curtain
opt.fortune.label [291c30] = 算命师的帘子
# en: A reading: she may point you towards something worth finding.
opt.fortune.hint [8515b5] = 算一卦：她也许会给你指一样值得去找的东西。
# en: She turns a card with a black wand on it. "A thing that bites," she says, "under a cloth, in a little square by a lake. It is waiting for a hand that won't flinch." Then she charges you and closes the curtain.
opt.fortune.say.1 [2531a5] = 她翻开一张画着黑色魔杖的牌。“一样会咬人的东西，”她说，“盖在布下，在湖边的一个小广场上。它在等一只不会缩回去的手。”然后她收了钱，拉上了帘子。
# en: She turns a card with a spoon on it, which you didn't know was a card. "An old man counting aloud," she says. "Count with him and something of his will be yours." Then she charges you.
opt.fortune.say.2 [711e7a] = 她翻开一张画着勺子的牌——你都不知道还有这种牌。“一个大声数数的老人，”她说，“跟他一起数，他的某样东西就会归你。”然后她收了钱。
# en: She turns a card with a lighthouse on it. "A little book of tides," she says, "kept by a man who loves the sea and lives inland. Ask him about the light." Then she charges you.
opt.fortune.say.3 [2ac7d4] = 她翻开一张画着灯塔的牌。“一本记潮汐的小书，”她说，“归一个爱海却住在内陆的人。问问他那盏灯的事。”然后她收了钱。
# en: She turns three cards, looks at them a long time and turns them back over. "You'll be fine," she says, which she has never said to anyone, according to her face. It's worth the money.
opt.fortune.say.4 [ce6428] = 她翻开三张牌，看了很久，又把它们翻了回去。“你会没事的，”她说——看她的表情，她从没对任何人这么说过。这钱花得值。
# en: The wandwright
opt.wandwright.label [e6eebb] = 魔杖匠
# en: New wands, re-cored in the capital, and a fair trade for the academy's loaner.
opt.wandwright.hint [6ba16a] = 在王都换过芯的新魔杖，学院借用杖也能公道地折价。
# en: {~The wandwright's door is scorched round the handle. Inside, sparks.|The wandwright looks up through a pair of smoked spectacles. "Come in. Don't touch anything that's humming."}
opt.wandwright.say.1 [a48caf] = {~魔杖匠的门把手周围一圈焦痕。里面火花四溅。|魔杖匠透过一副烟色眼镜抬起头。“进来。别碰任何在嗡嗡响的东西。”}
# en: Read the plates and walk on
opt.look.label [7e8ca4] = 读读铜牌，接着走
# en: {~You read every plate twice. One just says "No."|You walk the colonnade end to end and keep your coins. A tutor calls a fact after you, for free, out of habit.}
opt.look.say.1 [73edb2] = {~每块铜牌你都读了两遍。有一块只写着“不”。|你把柱廊从头走到尾，一个硬币也没花。一位家庭教师出于习惯，免费在你身后喊了一条知识。}

@event arcade_tutor
# en: The Tutor's Room
title [8b8795] = 家庭教师的房间
# en: Three tutors share the room and the rent: a thin one for spells and stars, a stout one for books and potions and a fierce small woman for "everything else, which is most things". They charge like surgeons. They're worth it, they say, and the queue outside suggests they might be.
text [b068a1] = 三位家庭教师合用这间屋子和房租：一个瘦的教法术和星象，一个胖的教书本和药剂，还有一个凶巴巴的小个子女人教“其他一切，也就是大部分东西”。他们收费像外科医生。他们说自己值这个价，门外的队伍表明他们也许没说错。
# en: A book-lined room off a colonnade, three tutors in shabby gowns at three desks, each pointing at a different chair.
scene [32fd57] = 柱廊旁一间满是书的房间，三位穿着旧袍子的家庭教师坐在三张桌子后，各自指着一把不同的椅子。
# en: Spellwork with the thin one
opt.arcana.label [43f876] = 跟瘦的那位练法术
# en: Arcana XP: a good deal of it.
opt.arcana.hint [142e5d] = 奥术经验：很多。
# en: He makes you cast the same light forty times, each a little cleaner, until your wand hand shakes and the fortieth light is the best you've ever made.
opt.arcana.say.1 [268597] = 他让你把同一盏光施放四十遍，一遍比一遍干净，直到你握杖的手发抖，而第四十盏是你施过最好的光。
# en: Books with the stout one
opt.lore.label [790819] = 跟胖的那位读书
# en: Lore XP: a good deal of it.
opt.lore.hint [87ec6f] = 学识经验：很多。
# en: He gives you three books, reads you the important page of each aloud and makes you argue with all three. You leave with a headache and a great deal more history.
opt.lore.say.1 [ce83b4] = 他给你三本书，把每本最要紧的一页读给你听，再逼你和这三本书逐一辩论。你离开时头痛欲裂，历史却多懂了一大截。
# en: Potions with the stout one
opt.alchemy.label [e43303] = 跟胖的那位学药剂
# en: Alchemy XP: a good deal of it.
opt.alchemy.hint [de37d8] = 炼金经验：很多。
# en: He brews in a teacup, at speed, talking all the while, and makes you do it after him. By the third cup you know more than a term of the textbook told you.
opt.alchemy.say.1 [648d0d] = 他用茶杯飞快地调制，一边调一边讲，再让你照着做。到第三杯时，你懂的已经比课本一学期教的还多。
# en: Manners with the fierce one
opt.charm.label [2ccf1e] = 跟凶的那位学礼仪
# en: Charm XP: a good deal of it.
opt.charm.hint [1aa14c] = 魅力经验：很多。
# en: She makes you walk into the room nine times until you do it right, then teaches you to say no so that people thank you for it. You leave walking differently.
opt.charm.say.1 [946c67] = 她让你走进房间九次，直到走对为止，然后教你怎样说“不”能让人反过来谢你。你离开时走路的样子都变了。
# en: The fierce one's drills
opt.vigor.label [f6c99a] = 凶的那位的操练
# en: Vigor XP: a good deal of it.
opt.vigor.hint [53b550] = 体魄经验：很多。
# en: She runs you up and down the colonnade until the bathhouse admirals come out to watch. You'll ache for a week, and you could climb a wall after it.
opt.vigor.say.1 [f7d0ca] = 她让你在柱廊里来回跑，跑到浴场的海军将领们都出来看。你会酸痛一个星期，练完之后你能翻墙。
# en: The fierce one's other lessons
opt.guile.label [cf3d0f] = 凶的那位的另一种课
# en: Guile XP: a good deal of it.
opt.guile.hint [1a7f9d] = 诡计经验：很多。
# en: She shuts the door and teaches you, briskly, how a liar's eyes move and how to keep your own still. "For your protection," she says, and charges extra.
opt.guile.say.1 [8552dd] = 她关上门，干脆利落地教你说谎者的眼睛怎么动，以及怎样让自己的眼睛不动。“为了保护你自己，”她说，然后多收了钱。
# en: Too dear today
opt.leave.label [5593e2] = 今天太贵了
# en: The three tutors go back to arguing about which of them you'd have chosen.
opt.leave.say.1 [dcc8d1] = 三位家庭教师又吵了起来，吵的是你本来会选哪一位。

@event arcade_scribe
# en: The Scribe's Window
title [987cb8] = 代笔人的窗口
# en: The scribe writes in a hand that makes "Dear" look like a promise. She'll write to anyone you name, in any style, and send it by the morning post. She'll also write you a letter of good character, she says, very quietly, if you need one and don't ask what it's worth.
text [15af58] = 代笔人的字写得能让“亲爱的”像一句承诺。你说出谁的名字，她就写给谁，什么文体都行，第二天早班邮车寄出。她还压低声音说，如果你需要，她也能写一封品行证明信，只要你别问它值多少。
# en: A scribe's desk in a sunny arcade window, inkpots and sealing wax, a woman with ink to the elbows writing a letter while a student dictates.
scene [c9bd84] = 阳光充足的拱廊窗边一张代笔人的桌子，墨水瓶和封蜡，一位墨水染到手肘的女人正在写信，一个学生在口述。
# en: A letter to Tobias
opt.tobias.label [068d87] = 写给托比亚斯
# en: Tobias is away from the capital; a letter keeps you close.
opt.tobias.hint [fe7aa9] = 托比亚斯不在王都；写封信，保持亲近。
# en: You tell him the capital's weather first, the way his mother would. His answer has a pressed flower in it and a long paragraph about mud, and you read it twice.
opt.tobias.say.1 [16d46e] = 你像他母亲那样，先跟他讲王都的天气。他的回信里夹着一朵压花，还有一长段关于泥巴的话，你读了两遍。
# en: A letter to Nessa
opt.nessa.label [eed4fb] = 写给内莎
# en: Nessa is away from the capital; a letter keeps you close.
opt.nessa.hint [123981] = 内莎不在王都；写封信，保持亲近。
# en: You send her the best gossip of the arcade, scribe's honour. Her answer asks for sources, dates and spellings, and says it's the best letter she's had all break.
opt.nessa.say.1 [6d958f] = 你把拱廊里最好的八卦寄给她，以代笔人的名誉担保。她回信要了消息来源、日期和拼写，说这是她整个假期收到的最好的信。
# en: A letter to Kael
opt.kael.label [0244c6] = 写给凯尔
# en: Kael is away from the capital; a letter keeps you close.
opt.kael.hint [1c7af0] = 凯尔不在王都；写封信，保持亲近。
# en: The scribe asks if the North gets letters at all. It does: Kael's answer comes with frost on the envelope and three careful lines, which from Kael is a great deal.
opt.kael.say.1 [cf1b5b] = 代笔人问北方到底收不收得到信。收得到：凯尔的回信信封上结着霜，里面写了仔细的三行——对凯尔来说，这已经很多了。
# en: A letter to Ilse
opt.ilse.label [d067a2] = 写给伊尔泽
# en: Ilse is away from the capital; a letter keeps you close.
opt.ilse.hint [8da554] = 伊尔泽不在王都；写封信，保持亲近。
# en: You write to Ilse and the scribe makes it warmer than you dared. Ilse's answer is one line, "You're strange," and a snowflake pressed between two sheets that hasn't melted.
opt.ilse.say.1 [ada77c] = 你给伊尔泽写信，代笔人把它写得比你敢写的更温暖。伊尔泽只回了一行：“你真奇怪。”两页纸之间夹着一片没有融化的雪花。
# en: A letter of good character
opt.character.label [784efd] = 一封品行证明信
# en: A forged reference from a respectable name: the prefect watching you stops. It's forgery.
opt.character.hint [77f360] = 一封以体面人名义伪造的推荐信：盯着你的级长不再盯了。这是伪造。
# en: The scribe writes you a reference from a magistrate who has never heard of you, in a magistrate's hand, with a magistrate's seal. Back at the castle the prefect reads it twice and stops following you about. Your conscience follows instead.
opt.character.say.1 [93583f] = 代笔人以一位从没听说过你的治安法官的名义、用治安法官的笔迹、盖着治安法官的印，给你写了一封推荐信。回到城堡，级长把信读了两遍，不再跟着你到处转了。换成你的良心跟着你。
# en: Write your own, at home
opt.own.label [ea927d] = 回去自己写
# en: You thank her and go. She goes back to the love letter in the window, which is going very well.
opt.own.say.1 [c04ef2] = 你道了谢离开。她又回到窗边那封情书上，那封信写得很顺利。

@event arcade_wandwright
# en: The Wandwright's
title [850645] = 魔杖匠的作坊
# en: The wandwright has burns on every finger and two wands behind the counter worth the trip: a glasscore, pale birch around a thread of capital glass that sparks with every spell, and a tidewood, salt-hard driftwood from the breakwater, re-cored, that makes a ward come smooth. "And I'll take the academy's loaners off you," she says. "They make good kindling."
text [422b08] = 魔杖匠的每根手指上都有烫伤，柜台后有两根值得专程来一趟的魔杖：一根玻璃芯，苍白的桦木裹着一缕王都玻璃，每个法术都会迸出火花；一根潮木，防波堤上盐浸坚硬的浮木，换过杖芯，能让护界升得顺滑。“学院的借用杖我也收，”她说，“当柴烧挺好。”
# en: A cramped workshop of wand blanks and humming racks, sparks in the air, a wandwright in smoked spectacles holding a pale wand up to the light.
scene [3571c3] = 狭窄的作坊里堆着魔杖坯料，架子嗡嗡作响，空中火花飞舞，一位戴烟色眼镜的魔杖匠把一根苍白的魔杖举向光。
# en: The glasscore wand
opt.glasscore.label [a3d35f] = 玻璃芯魔杖
# en: A wand for fights: every spell you cast also throws a spark of damage.
opt.glasscore.hint [c8b70b] = 战斗用魔杖：你施放的每个法术还会迸出一颗火花造成伤害。
# en: She puts it in your hand and says "Cast." You light a candle and a second spark leaps off the tip and lights the next one too. "It does that," she says. "Every time."
opt.glasscore.say.1 [721b20] = 她把它放进你手里，说：“施法。”你点亮一根蜡烛，杖尖又迸出第二颗火花，把旁边那根也点着了。“它就是这样，”她说，“每次都这样。”
# en: The tidewood wand
opt.tidewood.label [adc389] = 潮木魔杖
# en: A wand for fights: Ward costs less, and fire hurts you less.
opt.tidewood.hint [71120c] = 战斗用魔杖：护界更省，火焰伤你更轻。
# en: It's heavy for driftwood and smells of the harbour. You raise a ward with it and the ward comes up smooth and cool, like a wave going out.
opt.tidewood.say.1 [c61708] = 作为浮木它沉得出奇，闻起来是港口的味道。你用它升起一道护界，护界升得顺滑而清凉，像退去的浪。
# en: The tidewood, for your borrowed wand
opt.tidewood_swap.label [2c8fe5] = 用你的借用杖换潮木魔杖
# en: She takes the academy's loaner in part-exchange: Ward costs less, and fire hurts you less.
opt.tidewood_swap.hint [3a1615] = 她收下学院的借用杖抵一部分钱：护界更省，火焰伤你更轻。
# en: She snaps the borrowed wand's chipped tip off between finger and thumb, sniffs it and throws it on the kindling. The tidewood comes up smooth in your hand. "Better," she says. "Anything was."
opt.tidewood_swap.say.1 [aa1cab] = 她用拇指和食指掰下借用杖崩了角的杖尖，闻了闻，扔进柴堆。潮木在你手里顺滑地升起护界。“好多了，”她说，“换什么都会好些。”
# en: Just watch the sparks
opt.leave.label [8f7bc7] = 只是看看火花
# en: You watch her re-core a duchess's wand with tweezers and a bad temper. It's the best free thing in the capital.
opt.leave.say.1 [3ea9d8] = 你看着她用镊子和一肚子火气给一位公爵夫人的魔杖换芯。这是王都最好的免费节目。

@event arcade_waiting_room
# en: Waiting to Hear It
title [12a5b8] = 等着听那句话
# en: The fortune-teller's waiting room has three people on its bench: a widow, an old sea captain and a clerk. The captain says they're here every week, all three, waiting to hear the same thing they heard last week. "What are you waiting to hear?" the widow asks you. They all lean in.
text [7d4865] = 算命师的候客室里，长凳上坐着三个人：一位寡妇，一位老船长，一个文员。船长说他们三个每周都来，等着听上周听过的同一句话。“你在等着听什么？”寡妇问你。三个人都凑了过来。
# en: A small waiting room behind a beaded curtain, three people on a bench, a widow in black, an old sea captain and a nervous young clerk, all turning to look at a student.
scene [8efc5c] = 珠帘后的小候客室，长凳上坐着三个人——一位黑衣寡妇、一位老船长和一个紧张的年轻文员，都转头看着一个学生。
# en: Tell them the truth
opt.left.label [f3042a] = 跟他们说实话
# en: You tell them, and it's more than you meant to. The captain nods. The widow pats your hand. The clerk tells you his, which is about a girl at the post office. Nobody goes in when the curtain opens. You talk till the arcade shuts, and you feel lighter.
opt.left.say.1 [af317d] = 你说了，说得比你打算的多。船长点点头。寡妇拍拍你的手。文员说了他的，是关于邮局里的一个姑娘。帘子拉开时谁也没进去。你们一直聊到拱廊关门，你觉得轻松了。
# en: Read their palms yourself
opt.right.label [296435] = 亲自给他们看手相
# en: You read the captain's palm with great conviction: a long voyage, a dry harbour. The widow wants hers. The clerk pays you. The fortune-teller puts her head out, looks at you for a long moment, and goes back in.
opt.right.say.1 [09d86c] = 你煞有介事地给船长看手相：一次远航，一个干燥的港口。寡妇也要看。文员付了钱。算命师从帘子后探出头，盯着你看了好一会儿，又缩了回去。
# en: You tell the widow she'll marry soon. The captain coughs. The widow, it emerges, has been married three times and is here about the fourth. Everyone is very kind about it, which is the worst part.
opt.right.say.2 [bbce2d] = 你告诉寡妇她很快会结婚。船长咳了一声。原来寡妇已经结过三次婚，这回来问的是第四次。大家都对此非常体贴，这才是最糟的。

@event arcade_rival_tutors
# en: Two Tutors, Facing
title [96914c] = 对门的两位家庭教师
# en: Two tutors with doors facing across the colonnade have been feuding for twenty years, the bath-keeper tells you, over a pupil they once shared, who rose to be the Crown's chancellor and thanked only one of them in her memoirs. Each now shouts free sample lessons across the arcade at passing customers to show the other up. You are the passing customer. They both start at once.
text [d9ceb5] = 浴场的管理员告诉你，柱廊两边门对门的两位家庭教师已经斗了二十年，为的是他们共同教过的一个学生：她后来当上了王室的大法官，在回忆录里只感谢了其中一位。如今两人都隔着拱廊冲路过的客人喊免费试听课，好压对方一头。你就是那个路过的客人。他们同时开了口。
# en: Two tutors in shabby gowns in facing doorways across a stone colonnade, each shouting a free lesson at a student caught in the middle.
scene [336218] = 石柱廊两边对着的门口站着两位穿旧袍子的家庭教师，各自朝夹在中间的学生大喊一堂免费课。
# en: Stand in the middle and take both lessons
opt.left.label [cb3c94] = 站在中间，两堂课都听
# en: Two lectures at once, at full volume, on the law of the tides, the chancellor's favourite subject, from opposite sides. You come out knowing more about tides than any sailor, with a ringing in your ears that lasts till supper.
opt.left.say.1 [d0a237] = 两堂课同时开讲，音量拉满，讲的都是大法官最爱的潮汐定律，从两个方向。你出来时对潮汐的了解超过任何水手，耳朵一直嗡嗡响到晚饭。
# en: Ask which of them she thanked
opt.right.label [75f5ad] = 问她感谢的是哪一位
# en: Both stop. Neither, it turns out, has read the memoirs. They spend an hour looking for the page together in the bath-keeper's copy, and you spend the hour holding the lamp. She thanked the bath-keeper. They go out for a drink together, appalled.
opt.right.say.1 [4a485d] = 两人都停住了。原来谁也没读过那本回忆录。他们在浴场管理员的那本里一起找了一个小时，你在旁边举了一个小时的灯。她感谢的是浴场管理员。两人吓坏了，一起出去喝了一杯。

@event arcade_admirals_hot_room
# en: The Admirals' Bench
title [2fb91a] = 将军们的长凳
# en: In the bathhouse's hot room, a bench of retired admirals in towels are having their weekly wager: who can stay longest in the heat. The oldest moves up to make room for you. "Fresh blood," he says. "The academy, eh? Let's see what they're teaching you."
text [206d47] = 浴场的热房里，一排裹着毛巾的退休海军将领正在进行每周的赌赛：谁能在热气里待得最久。最年长的那位挪了挪给你腾出位置。“新鲜血液，”他说，“学院来的，嗯？看看他们都教了你什么。”
# en: A tiled bathhouse hot room thick with steam, a row of red-faced retired admirals in towels on a bench, one making room for a student.
scene [9bf75f] = 蒸汽弥漫的瓷砖热房，一排脸红通通、裹着毛巾的退休海军将领坐在长凳上，其中一位正给一个学生腾位置。
# en: Sit it out with them
opt.left.label [777f0e] = 和他们一起坐到底
# en: You outlast four admirals and a commodore and stagger out last into the cold plunge, to applause. The oldest admiral writes your name on the bathhouse slate, under three admirals and a duke, and invites you to dinner.
opt.left.say.1 [691ad7] = 你熬过了四位将军和一位准将，最后一个踉跄着冲进冷水池，赢得一片掌声。最年长的将军把你的名字写在浴场的石板上，排在三位将军和一位公爵下面，还邀请你去吃晚饭。
# en: You last until the room starts to spin, and are carried out to the cold plunge by two admirals who tell you about the time they were carried out too. You lie in the cool room for an hour, pink and humbled.
opt.left.say.2 [c01413] = 你一直坚持到房间开始旋转，被两位将军抬去了冷水池，他们给你讲了自己当年也被抬出去的事。你在凉房里躺了一个小时，浑身发红，满心惭愧。
# en: Go straight to the cold plunge
opt.right.label [c62286] = 直接去冷水池
# en: You take the cold plunge instead, with a yell the admirals applaud. It's like being hit by the sea. You come out awake to your fingertips and a little ashamed you didn't stay.
opt.right.say.1 [5fab98] = 你改去冷水池，大叫一声跳了进去，将军们为这一声鼓掌。像被大海迎面撞了一下。你出来时清醒到了指尖，又有点惭愧自己没留下。
